  "interpretation": [
    "Each run offered 4,800 requests below the 6,000-per-minute caller budget. The first unprofiled run had nine HTTP 503 responses in control-before; its unprofiled repeat had none.",
    "The first profiled run had one HTTP 503 in account-detail-overlap; its repeat had none. In the first profiled run, every PostgreSQL client stage recorded 1,599 successful samples and zero errors in that phase, matching the 1,599 successful HTTP responses. This places the missing request outside the instrumented PostgreSQL client path, but does not identify which earlier request/admission step rejected it.",
    "Across successful measured phases, scheduled p95 ranged from 4.60 ms to 7.41 ms; overlap was slower than adjacent controls by about 2.1–2.6 ms in the clean repeats. Sampled runtime connections peaked at eight or nine, with no sampled active-lock wait.",
    "These four short local runs do not establish capacity, production latency, an SLO, or a stable error rate. Profiling adds work. Keep the earlier ten-second 503 outcome visible; no security, admission, cache, or connection-pool setting was changed.",
    "The Compose runtime-role measurement is complete for this local workload. Kubernetes scheduling and replicated deployment evidence remain deferred."
  ]
}
